Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.00,Body,,0,0,0,,{\b1\fs36\c&H00D3EE&}Discord Reaction & Poll Role Manager{\r}\N\NOne-shot CLI - it exits after one run\N\NADD or REMOVE a role for:\N  * message reactors\N  * native Discord poll voters\N\NDeduplicates users and excludes bots by default
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:12.00,Body,,0,0,0,,{\b1\fs36\c&H00D3EE&}REAL SERVER COMMAND{\r}\N\N$ discord-role-manager\N    --message-url "https://discord.com/channels/GUILD/CHANNEL/MESSAGE"\N    --role-id ROLE_ID --action ADD --dry-run\N\NCredentials come only from DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN.\NRemove --dry-run after reviewing the preview.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.00,0:00:18.00,Body,,0,0,0,,{\b1\fs36\c&H00D3EE&}OFFLINE CORE DEMO - NO CREDENTIALS{\r}\N\N$ python demo_offline.py\N\NCollected unique humans: alice, bob, carol\NADDED  alice (101)\NSKIP   bob (102)  role already present\NADDED  carol (103)\N\NResult: discovered=3 changed=2 skipped=1 failed=0
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.00,0:00:24.00,Body,,0,0,0,,{\b1\fs36\c&H00D3EE&}AUTOMATED VERIFICATION{\r}\N\N$ pytest -q\N...........                                      [100%]\N11 passed\N\N$ ruff check .\NAll checks passed!\N\NCovers reactions, poll voters, deduplication, bot exclusion,\NADD/REMOVE, skips, dry-run, and URL parsing.
